    "appInfoTitle": "Application Information",
    "faq": {
      "q1": "How do I create a portfolio?",
      "a1": "Go to the 'Portfolios' page from the left menu. Click the 'New Portfolio' button at the top right. You can create one by entering a portfolio name, description and currency.",
      "q2": "How do I add an instrument to a portfolio?",
      "a2": "Click the 'Add Transaction' button on the portfolio detail page. Search for an instrument and enter the quantity and price to add a buy or sell transaction.",
      "q3": "Which currencies can I use?",
      "a3": "You can select TRY, USD or EUR when creating a portfolio. All calculations are automatically converted according to your selected currency.",
      "q4": "How do I compare instruments?",
      "a4": "Go to the 'Comparison' page from the left menu. Select two instruments and set the time range. Charts and performance metrics are calculated automatically.",
      "q5": "What is the watchlist for?",
      "a5": "You can add instruments to your watchlist using the 'Follow' button on the instrument detail page. You can view the instruments you follow on the Watchlist page in the left menu.",
      "q6": "Where does historical price data come from?",
      "a6": "Historical price data is fetched from Yahoo Finance. TCMB archive data is used for exchange rates. 1 year of historical data is available.",
      "q7": "What happens if I delete a transaction?",
      "a7": "Transactions are soft deleted, meaning the data is not lost but is excluded from calculations."
    },
